# FS.GG.SDD — regenerable lifecycle output (ADR-0018).
# Per-work-item readiness views are generated by fsgg-sdd and regenerated by
# `fsgg-sdd refresh`. They are transient: ignore by role, never commit, and do
# not re-include per feature. See docs/reference/artifact-taxonomy.md.
readiness/*/

# Generic build & tooling output.
bin/
obj/
artifacts/
TestResults/
.tmp/
nuget-cache/

# ADR-0067 §9 phase 4 stage 3 (FS-GG/.github#1720). A GENERATED VIEW of .claude/skills, resolved at
# checkout by `scripts/skill-view generate` and never committed: a committed symlink checks out as a
# plain text file under `git -c core.symlinks=false` (the git-for-Windows default without Developer
# Mode) and BOTH agent runtimes then load zero skills and exit 0 saying nothing (ADR-0067 §6). The
# FS.GG.Kit materialize regenerates it and then asserts it is visible (FsggKitCheckSkillView,
# ADR-0067 §8), and scripts/check-skill-view-roots.sh asserts the root is still in the contract.
/.agents/skills
